      <Parameters>
        <Parameter Name="shouldLoopAnimation" Type="System.Boolean" />
      </Parameters>
      <Docs>
        <param name="shouldLoopAnimation"><see langword="true" /> to request repetition or continued animation within system limits; <see langword="false" /> for normal non-looping playback.</param>
        <summary>Sets whether the state icon animation should repeat.</summary>
        <returns>This builder.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>With looping enabled, the system limits repetitions of finite animations and the run time of infinite animations. Finite animations normally finish before a state change unless the next state requests interruption; infinite animations can stop at any frame.</para>
          <para>With looping disabled, finite animations play once, subject to system limits, and infinite animations run briefly, for about three seconds. Static icons ignore this setting.</para>
        </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
